From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:58:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hamoa: Power the display GDSC while the
 camera runs

CAMSS on X1E80100 delivers no frames once the display subsystem has been
powered down for a while, although the sensor is programmed over CCI and
CSID starts. Holding MDSS_GDSC on brings the frames back, with the panel
off, MMCX at low_svs and the rest of the display subsystem suspended.
Raising MXC, MMCX or MX, or holding GCC_DISP_HF_AXI_CLK or the eDP PHY
supplies, does not.

List MDSS_GDSC as a third power domain of the camera clock controller.
Its top-level GDSC then becomes a subdomain of MDSS_GDSC, so the display
GDSC is on whenever TITAN_TOP_GDSC is.

Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
index 2e72fa8..e00b48f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
@@ -5821,7 +5821,8 @@ camcc: clock-controller@ade0000 {
 				 <&bi_tcxo_ao_div2>,
 				 <&sleep_clk>;
 			power-domains = <&rpmhpd RPMHPD_MXC>,
-					<&rpmhpd RPMHPD_MMCX>;
+					<&rpmhpd RPMHPD_MMCX>,
+					<&dispcc MDSS_GDSC>;
 			required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_low_svs>,
 					<&rpmhpd_opp_low_svs>;
 			#clock-cells = <1>;
